Z||000000||Patrick's Dad||10-05-2001||10:03 PM|||| <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=595911291&r=0&t=0" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=595911291&r=0&t=0</A> <P>This auction is for a pair of worked over heads. They look like the iron heads, but I'm not an expert. I'm not going to bid here, but I'm curious, because the company is less than an hour away.<P>I plan a pretty straightforward 3.4 shortblock with Silv-o-lite pistons and Crower SBC c/r's (Yes, I know about oversized bearings), ARP's, etc. I've been planning on ported intake and polished GIII Aluminum heads, rollers, and possibly a worked over 3400 intake setup.<P>If these are the iron heads, they should mate up with the Fiero intake. Will/can they come close to claims? There won't be a radical cam, this needs to be streetable, but worthy of respect when the hammer's been dropped. Maybe to take the pink slip of a stock "5.0"<P>For $250ish, they look good, but are they too good to be true?||||reg||1
Z||000001||samoht||10-05-2001||10:12 PM||||they are iron heads.. I dont beleive the claims of 300 hp.. maybe at the crank...  I dont doubt you could make 300 horses, bu twill a 3.4 stay together is the question, push let alone streetable....  Seems like a good deal though..  I like the large vavle fiero head, I would work on headers and keep the stock ones streetable.. push he was talking about the mill work, who knbow what compression ratio you would end up with, I took 10/10 off and I run 3.1 pistons at around 9:1 .. they were .017 at TDC to the deck surface... ( but I milled my deck .010)  all and all the machine work alone is 500 dollars.. but I think it is way more than any street car should have.. hope this helps||||reg||1
